  "report": {
    "incident_title": "Search results missing products / some searches fail",
    "outcome": "conclusive",
    "summary": "Search degradation is caused by the loss of Elasticsearch data node es-data-3 (AWS hardware status-check failure at 15:17Z). The products index has no replicas, so the two primary shards that lived on es-data-3 became unassigned and have no copy to fail over to. Searches that touch those shards return partial results (missing products, which is consistent with whole brands dropping out) or fail outright. The cause is a 2026-09-16 cost-saving change that reindexed products with number_of_replicas=0, with replica re-enablement still open as SRCH-311. The web-frontend v12.3.0 release at 15:00Z is a footer-only change that does not touch the search path; the timing does not fit it and it is not the cause. No alert fired during the window, so this was detected by users first.",
    "root_cause": "Single data-node hardware failure (es-data-3, 15:17Z) on an Elasticsearch index created with zero replicas (change 2026-09-16 \"Reindex products into new cluster with number_of_replicas=0\", follow-up SRCH-311 never completed). Two of the 10 primary shards of 'products' became unassigned, so search-svc's queries against them failed or returned partial results.",
    "confidence": "high",
    "hypotheses": [
      {
        "rank": 1,
        "hypothesis_id": "H1",
        "statement": "es-data-3 hardware failure removed 2 primary shards of 'products' that had no replicas; searches touching them fail or return partial results (missing brands).",
        "status": "supported",
        "confidence": "high",
        "supporting_evidence": [
          "E1",
